A||||4||CanadianGT||Finally got Fire damaged GT back||||1||
Z||000000||CanadianGT||07-17-2001||12:57 PM||||Well I paid all my money into court($3600 for a 2100 quoted job),and finally got my Fiero Back.  Of course I could not drive it back, as they could still not properly rebuild my engine after 3 and a half months, so I got CAA to tow it for me.  The fire damage has been cleaned off the outside , but it still stinks.  So bad in fact, that when I got up this morning and went in my Garage, the whole place smelt like smoke, and even the inside of my dad's Jag did too!  Looks like my baby will be sleeping outside in the driveway for awhile  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">.  On top of all that, it looks like they reinstalled my alternator wrong as it is touching the cv joint!!  They also never put my  heat shield back on the exaust manifold by the firewall.  Also he charged me on the final bill with having to reinstall the computer, but he did not do it properly and it was hanging from the wires, and he did not put the console back.  He left it in the passenger seat. I have pics off all this stuff, and a scanner, but I do not know how to put them on here.  I have to still wait for a court date to be set, but I sure am looking forward to getting justice.  <BR>Kyle  ||||reg||1
Z||000001||Oreif||07-17-2001||01:18 PM||||I would also get an estimate on steam cleaning the interior and/or replacing items that have smoke damage. They should pay for that since they didn't have insurance. It could get very expensive to replace smoke damaged interior parts. (Carpet, Headliner, seats, Door panels,etc) Who knows, by the time they add up all the damaged items, you might end up with a Mr.Mikes interior!||||reg||1
Z||000002||rogergarrison||07-17-2001||03:02 PM||||go to an auto detailer. they have a liquid that absorbs those odors. just soak a few cotton balls and put them under your seat and leave the windows closed. You might try an open package of baking soda left inside too.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Cheever2||07-17-2001||03:08 PM||||Who knows, you just might end up owning the shop!  They sure don't deserve it.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000004||Jay||07-17-2001||04:15 PM||||did I miss something?  What happened?  I know a good interior guy if you are interested, he's in Scarborough.  I work in hardwood flooring and people are always complaining about the smell.  One thing that works is to cut an onion or two into a bucket of water and leave it in the car over night.  Works with fumes anyways.<P>------------------<BR>Jay<BR>1986 Northstar GT<BR>www.members.home.net/jaygrande<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/cayuga3_3.jpg"> ||||reg||1
